course: dictionary
lesson: 16016
title: Vocabulary: vegetation
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Vegetation means all the plants that grow in a place, taken together. That includes trees, bushes, grass and flowers. It is one word for the whole green covering of an area, not just one plant.
explain: «The rainforest had thick vegetation everywhere.» Thick tells you there is a lot of it. «Deserts have very little vegetation.» Little tells you there are only a few plants. Look for words like thick, lush, sparse and little to work out how much vegetation there is.
explain: Vegetation is an uncountable noun, so you do not count it. Write some vegetation, not three vegetations. Common phrases are natural vegetation, lush vegetation, sparse vegetation and vegetation cover.
fact: Vegetation means all the plants that grow in a place.
fact: «Lush» vegetation is thick, healthy and green.
fact: «Sparse» vegetation is thin and spread far apart.
fact: Rainforests have thick vegetation, while deserts and tundra have little vegetation.
fact: Vegetation gives food and shelter to animals, and it helps hold soil together, which stops erosion and floods.
exercise: «The rainforest had thick vegetation everywhere.» What does vegetation mean here? | All the animals living there | *All the plants growing there | The rivers that flow through it | The weather in the rainforest
exercise: «Deserts have very little vegetation, so few plants can grow.» Which word tells you how much vegetation there is? | Plants | Deserts | *little | Grow
exercise: Why is vegetation important to animals? | It makes the weather hotter | It stops animals from moving | It is a kind of rock | *It gives them food and shelter
test: Which phrase means the plants are thin and spread far apart? | *sparse vegetation | lush vegetation | thick vegetation | natural vegetation
test: Which phrase would best describe a jungle full of plants? | little vegetation | vegetation cover of rock | *thick vegetation | sparse vegetation
exam: «The hills were covered in lush vegetation after the spring rain.» What does vegetation mean in this sentence? | The rain that falls on the hills | *All the plants growing on the hills | The rocks at the top of the hills | The soil under the hills
